# Coordinator handoff and review

## How can two investigators distinguish these readings?

When independently written implementations return the same token, what stronger observations distinguish the same computation from a coincidental match? Edition 02 Paper III asked for a counterexample, operative repair and rerun after a disputed transition. Gemini supplied a seven-page independent written review of Papers I-III on 27 November 2026. This local author proposes three amendments. The supplied review stays intact with the private editions. Its verdict concerned Edition 02; local independent disposition of 02.1 requires its own source examination and measured evidence.

For A1, the disputed input is a private duplicate selecting the second readout. The older listing decodes and commits the stock result. Check both private scores, histories and selected update/token/guard; zero commits and a second-branch tuple discriminate the amended reading. For A2, put a NaN at a raw ID that the page guard later suppresses. The previous final-only validity equation can pass; the first failing amended cut is raw. Add a signed-zero bit flip to a permitted word and an independently illegal page edit. Retain every conflict at its own cut. For C1, a 9:1 first reading of two equally plausible tables leaves the maximum at 0.9. Repeating those bytes cannot cross 0.95. Stop unresolved unless a fresh informative source exists. Compare action, posterior, positive gain and stop status, in addition to any chosen ID.

The finite test takes one label-free JSON object. The wrapper binds its unmodified input bytes by SHA-256 to a scheduled row. Freeze source, independent predictions, source pins, input commitments and the normal command before any blind comparison. Compare the complete typed return and its digest on each row, counting missing, failed and mismatched returns as zero. Keep denominators A1=6, A2=6, C1=8 apart; historical 24 vector lines and 448 projected correction checks are another experiment. One result set cannot raise the score in another. Agreement on those observations is a finite conclusion about the frozen entries.

The predecessor's proposed admission predicate requires a received cloud review, discharged objections and adequate required evidence per claim. The local coordinator decides disposition. A separate reviewer writes a fresh evaluator, freezes it, executes the committed inputs, then inspects the authors' sources, papers and relay of the original evidence. The fixture owner commits an independent oracle before exposure. Preserve adverse or mixed outcomes before disclosure. A single wrong field exposes a concrete counterexample; any repair needs another freeze and checks. Distinguish an author's derivation, Gemini's original written observations, the new review and a local release.

The creator/writer observation in Q1 remains a separate host question. Under the stated trusted cooperating components an identifying creation event and bounded writer set may justify a claim for their observed interval; a stronger unobserved-writer model leaves the exclusivity claim unresolved. No direct-launch result enters A1, A2 or C1. The archived WP-0043 verdict is M with 0/5 qualified rows; WP-0044 found 0/2 genuine positives per route and complete expected records 14/33 and 13/33. Native state replay, model efficacy, device availability and other-concept releases are unmeasured here.

The bound predecessor's pp. 1-5 retain full observation, change and review protocols under the three replacements below. The smallest follow-up decision uses independent exact finite records and verified attachment inventories. If author and reviewer disagree, name the first divergent input, field and proof premise. Qualify each correction individually before considering any larger experiment.

endstream
